WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.750
All right, next let's talk about volume.

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:04.350
Because, for a lot of beginners, this is

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:06.470
what I would recommend people focus on

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:07.950
more than quality, more than thinking

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:09.430
about whether this post is useful or

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:11.550
not. For you to really be successful and

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:13.550
to get the ball rolling, you need to get

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.230
reps. You need to get repetitions in

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.470
order for you to get better at this. And

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:18.790
just to get you in the right frame of

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.790
mind when it comes to volume, one

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:22.470
question that I get a lot is the

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:24.630
question around how much should I post

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:26.750
or how much can I post? And my simple

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.430
answer to that is as many as you humanly

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:31.310
can. There's a couple of reasons why I

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.350
hold that as sage advice when it comes

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:35.070
to volume. The first one is, as we

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:36.390
already mentioned in the previous

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.110
module, is that no one really cares what

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:39.670
you post, especially when you're just

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:41.630
starting. As long as it's not something

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.270
illegal or something that will get you

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:45.070
flamed, just post something that you

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:46.990
think is useful. The second thing is

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:48.630
that all these social media platforms,

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:51.190
Instagram, TikTok, Twitter, everything

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:53.110
else, they don't really have a cap on

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:54.830
how much you can post. And just to prove

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:56.470
this point, there is this Instagram

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:58.470
page, it's called Instant Bollywood, and

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:00.110
you can check them out. They have 44

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.350
million followers. And what they do is

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:05.830
they post 100 times a day, 100 times.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:07.550
And because of their size, obviously,

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:09.350
Instagram already took notice of them.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:10.190
And when they had, I guess,

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.710
conversations or consulted with

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:13.470
Instagram, if that's okay, Instagram was

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:16.070
okay with 100 posts per day for one

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.190
account. So, that's how extreme these

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:19.670
things can get. But obviously, you don't

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:21.670
need to do 100 posts a day because

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:23.110
Instant Bollywood is a news brand, it

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:24.830
has a team. But this is just to prove

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:26.310
the point that you can post as many

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:27.670
times as you want and you won't get

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:29.750
punished, at least algorithm-wise. And

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.630
so, really my advice on volume is for

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:33.430
you to post as many as you can. Now, if

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:35.270
that number is only once a day or once a

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:37.310
week, then that's completely okay. But

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:38.950
just know that someone posting once a

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:41.390
week will get there much slower versus

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.070
someone who is posting once a day. It's

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.070
just a matter of math. To give you a

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:46.510
rule of thumb, at least for me,

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:48.270
especially in the beginning, my starting

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:50.310
rule back then when I was posting shorts

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:52.510
is that I wanted to hit at least three

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:54.230
per day. And the way I did that is by

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:56.350
having really low production quality in

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:58.630
terms of the video, but just optimizing

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:00.630
around making sure that what I am saying

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:02.190
and what I am featuring is actually

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.150
useful. So, if you browse my oldest

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:06.390
videos here, it's all just me talking

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:08.109
about stuff on AI that I found was

00:02:08.119 --> 00:02:09.910
useful. And I was doing like three per

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:11.350
day. And especially in the beginning

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:13.310
during these times, I was editing them

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:15.030
manually and posting them on TikTok

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:17.110
manually, which I also advise for you to

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.150
do. We'll get into more automation in

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:20.710
just a bit, but it's actually still

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:23.070
really useful for you to start posting

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:25.430
stuff manually from your phone to TikTok

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:27.550
and Instagram. Maybe edit a bit on

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:29.070
TikTok directly, just so that you can

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:31.070
get a sense of how to do them manually

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:32.670
before you expand outward and make

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:34.510
things faster to automation, which will

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.670
anyway cover. Another creator who does

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:38.150
this really well, at least on the volume

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:40.230
side, is Sabrina. So, you can see she

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:41.870
has 1.1 million followers now on

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:43.670
Instagram. I think she has a bit more on

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.470
TikTok. And I remember back then when

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:47.030
she was starting, she was saying how she

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:48.949
was posting, I think three to five times

00:02:48.959 --> 00:02:50.990
per day. And the way she's doing that is

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.150
kind of similar. You So, you can see

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:53.990
it's just her sometimes in her home,

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.910
maybe sometimes outside, and just off on

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:58.990
her phone's camera talking about stuff

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.790
that she is finding useful. So, again,

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:03.110
back to that point, that quality doesn't

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:05.030
really mean production value. It usually

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:07.550
means how useful your stuff is. So, yes,

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:09.509
try to target the most volume that you

00:03:09.519 --> 00:03:11.070
can. Again, if you can do one every

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:13.229
other day, given the nature of the work

00:03:13.239 --> 00:03:14.470
that you do, then that's completely

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:15.949
fine. But just know that someone who is

00:03:15.959 --> 00:03:17.870
posting three times a day will get there

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:19.790
faster usually. The other important

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:22.190
point around why volume is the key for

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:24.310
success, especially in the beginning and

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:26.509
even as you actually scale up, volume

00:03:26.519 --> 00:03:28.350
still matters quite a lot, is because it

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:30.509
forces you to iterate. But I did want to

00:03:30.519 --> 00:03:32.830
call out iteration, because if you post

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:34.910
one video and you just repeat that same

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:36.830
pattern without learning from it, then

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:38.670
you probably won't improve and you won't

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:40.229
be able to make it with your content.

00:03:40.239 --> 00:03:41.990
Because if you just target to do 100

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.949
videos without the awareness that you

00:03:43.959 --> 00:03:45.750
should improve every time that you post

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:47.310
a video, then for sure you'll be stuck

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:49.750
at low followership, unfortunately. But

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:51.350
the thing is, for most people, the more

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:53.070
that you do something, the more that you

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:54.550
learn. But just being aware that you do

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:56.030
need to iterate, and just improve

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:57.670
something in your videos every time,

00:03:57.680 --> 00:03:59.230
that's going to pay dividends for you

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:00.990
down the line because of how much the

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.990
quality of your videos compound. And so

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:04.350
now is that brings us to the second

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:06.350
framework that I wanted to introduce to

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:08.070
you, which is the content pyramid.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:09.190
Because remember, in the previous

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:10.830
modules, we talked about the content

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:12.990
trifecta, which is essentially the North

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:14.750
Star that you should have in terms of

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:16.310
the type of content that you should

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:17.870
produce. It needs to be something that

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:19.710
you enjoy or like, something that others

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:21.349
are finding useful, and something that

00:04:21.359 --> 00:04:23.270
is unique to you. But the thing is, you

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:24.990
probably won't get there in your very

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.870
first content. But the great news is,

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:28.790
when it comes to content, posting it is

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:30.630
free, and you almost have unlimited

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:32.790
tries in order to get to this sweet

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:34.710
spot. And so the content pyramid is a

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:36.909
very simple framework for how you can

00:04:36.919 --> 00:04:38.950
get there. We'll expand this later, but

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:41.070
for now, what I want you to focus on is

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:43.150
volume, again, as many as you humanly

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:44.990
can given the nature of your work and

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:46.350
other priorities that you have in your

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:48.470
life. And the second priority for you is

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:50.550
to improve, and to try new things per

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:52.909
video or per post. And when I talk about

00:04:52.919 --> 00:04:54.990
improve, especially in the beginning, I

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:56.909
actually don't want you to focus on

00:04:56.919 --> 00:04:59.270
small improvements to your video, like

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:01.030
changing the caption a bit or changing

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:02.909
your thumbnails a bit. You can obviously

00:05:02.919 --> 00:05:04.510
optimize that as you go, which is

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:05.950
completely fine. But if you haven't

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:07.909
gained traction yet, it's actually more

00:05:07.919 --> 00:05:10.790
useful for you to iterate more massively

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:12.390
in the beginning. And to give an example

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:14.390
from my experience, again, if you sort

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:16.950
by oldest from my oldest videos in here,

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:18.950
you may notice that in the beginning I

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:21.390
had like four videos in here that I

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:23.430
started posting and got something like

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:25.510
2,000 views. So that told me that

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:27.710
something was there, but my fifth video

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:29.909
had 900,000 views. So that really told

00:05:29.919 --> 00:05:31.790
me that I was onto something. But the

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:33.390
truth is, these are actually not the

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:35.390
very first Robo Nuggets branded post

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:37.110
that I made. Because when I started Robo

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:39.030
Nuggets, it was actually first a

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:40.630
newsletter. So you can see one of my

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:43.390
very first post was posted March 22nd of

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.590
2024, which is something like, I think

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:47.630
four months prior to my very first

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:50.150
TikTok post. But what I was testing is

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:51.630
the stuff that I was already listening

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:53.470
to, like this podcast from Lex. I

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:55.150
basically just summarize it, post it in

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:57.030
this blog, and then I think I started

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:59.230
posting it on Reddit or other forums

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:01.510
that I think these types of summaries

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:03.190
would be useful in. Now, I did this

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:05.070
newsletter approach for I think a few

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:06.670
articles, but then I quickly realized

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:08.510
that I'm not getting the traction that I

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:10.230
need. And now that I look back, it sort

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:11.870
of makes sense because with newsletters,

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:13.990
they don't really have an algorithm, a

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.150
content algorithm to help you find the

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:17.710
people who will like your stuff. So,

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:19.909
even if I'm posting this, it probably

00:06:19.919 --> 00:06:22.430
won't get into the right people's pages

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:25.110
organically because it is just there in

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:26.950
the web without a way to discover them.

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:28.190
And so, the point I'm making here is

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:29.750
that it would probably have been better

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:31.909
for me to shift really quickly from a

00:06:31.919 --> 00:06:34.110
newsletter format and iterate into

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:35.710
something massively different, in which

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:37.670
case for me, that was TikTok. And so, my

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:39.470
advice to you is that yes, you need to

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:41.190
post as many as you can and just focus

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:42.870
on volume at the start. But if things

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:44.390
aren't working out, when you think about

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:46.390
iteration, especially in this stage when

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:47.870
you don't have a big followership yet,

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:49.550
you actually have a lot of freedom to

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:51.790
try out new things in order to find the

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:53.870
one that works best for you. So, try out

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:55.510
different channels, try out different

00:06:55.520 --> 00:06:57.790
formats, try out different ways by which

00:06:57.800 --> 00:06:59.390
you can present your content because the

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:01.350
best way for you to get to this point,

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:03.110
especially this green circle of finding

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:04.750
something that is unique to you, that

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:07.430
will come from volume and iteration.

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:09.710
Now, one mini experiment that helped me

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:11.430
out and uh is probably something that

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:13.110
you can try out as well, is to just set

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:15.750
a goal to ship your first 100 content

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:17.750
pieces. And what would be useful is if

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:19.310
you can put a counter, like literally

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:21.150
check boxes that you can tick off. If

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:22.830
you have a notebook that you use a lot,

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:24.550
then use that. I definitely did this

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:26.310
myself, especially when I was starting

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:27.830
where I have a board where I was ticking

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:29.590
off how many shorts that I published

00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:31.990
during that week up until I get to 100.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:33.510
And that will just give you a lot of

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:35.590
reps in terms of publishing content so

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:37.830
that you can get to your goal faster.

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:39.070
And it's also just naturally more

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:41.190
motivating for us as people if you

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:43.430
gamify this a bit so that the task of

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:45.670
doing 100 content pieces, even though

00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:47.350
that sounds daunting, it actually

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:49.590
becomes much easier once you see it in

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:51.590
one page and how close you are getting.

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:53.110
Once you just start posting content to

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:55.270
get to that 100. So, we've established

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:56.910
that volume is the key thing that you

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:58.630
need to focus on right now. We've also

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:00.150
established how important it is to

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:02.510
iterate as you move forward and that you

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:04.310
can worry about quality once you've

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:06.070
already built a following. So, the next

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:07.590
step now is for you to find good ideas

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:09.070
for content which would help you with

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:13.160
that volume which we will tackle next.
